abstract: >-
  Single-file, bilingual (English/Portuguese) browser application that prepares
  settlement-plate campaign photographs for annotation: campaign metadata from
  EXIF/GPS with optional weather retrieval, per-plate triage, four-corner homography
  cropping at fixed physical scale, and output of annotation-ready images, an
  import-ready metadata table, a triage map, a crop manifest recording the four
  source corners of every crop, and the physical scale embedded in every JPEG (JFIF
  density) plus an ImageJ calibration macro. v1.1.0 decodes photographs at native
  resolution and renders every pixel through the exact homography.
keywords:
  - benthic image analysis
  - biofouling
  - settlement plates
  - homography
  - percent cover
  - point count
  - image preprocessing
  - CoralNet
